\begin{abstract}
We construct a mathematical framework in which universes are modeled as 
canonically stable field configurations on $\mathbb{R}^4$. A canonical 
stability operator is defined, along with a variational principle, a 
canonical stability partial differential equation, and the classification 
of stable attractor solutions. Projection operators and rendering maps 
are introduced to visualize 4D canonical universes in lower-dimensional 
spaces. This document formalizes the structure of canonical universes 
and provides explicit stable solutions.
