\section{Complexity Bounds and Stability}

In this appendix we justify the canonical complexity constraint


\[
C_{\min} < C[\phi_\ast] < C_{\max},
\]


where


\[
C[\phi_\ast]
=
-\sum_{\ell,m} p_{\ell m} \log p_{\ell m},
\qquad
p_{\ell m}
=
\frac{|a_{\ell m}|^2}{\sum_{\ell',m'} |a_{\ell' m'}|^2}.
\]



\subsection{Interpretation of $p_{\ell m}$}

The coefficients $p_{\ell m}$ form a probability distribution over the 
active harmonic modes:


\[
p_{\ell m} \ge 0,
\qquad
\sum_{\ell,m} p_{\ell m} = 1.
\]



Thus $C[\phi_\ast]$ is the Shannon entropy of the harmonic spectrum.

\subsection{Lower Bound: Avoiding Triviality}

If only a single mode is active, say $(\ell_0,m_0)$, then


\[
p_{\ell_0 m_0} = 1,
\qquad
p_{\ell m} = 0 \text{ for all others}.
\]



Thus


\[
C[\phi_\ast] = 0.
\]



Such a configuration is overly simple and fails to satisfy the 
recursion and coherence requirements of canonical stability.  
Therefore we impose


\[
C[\phi_\ast] > C_{\min} > 0.
\]



\subsection{Upper Bound: Avoiding Overcomplexity}

If infinitely many modes contribute with equal weight, then


\[
p_{\ell m} = \frac{1}{M},
\qquad
M \to \infty.
\]



Then


\[
C[\phi_\ast]
= \log M
\to \infty.
\]



Such configurations are unstable because:

\begin{itemize}
    \item coherence breaks down,
    \item recursion symmetry is lost,
    \item the field becomes chaotic under perturbations.
\end{itemize}

Thus we impose


\[
C[\phi_\ast] < C_{\max},
\]


for some finite $C_{\max}$ determined by the stability operator.

\subsection{Existence of a Stable Band}

Let $S$ be the set of all harmonic spectra satisfying the amplitude 
constraints


\[
a_{\ell m} \propto \frac{1}{\ell(\ell+2)}.
\]



Then the induced probability distributions $p_{\ell m}$ satisfy


\[
0 < C_{\min} < C[\phi_\ast] < C_{\max} < \infty.
\]



This follows from:

\begin{itemize}
    \item the suppression of high-$\ell$ modes,
    \item the finite multiplicity $d_\ell = (\ell+1)^2$,
    \item the normalization of the amplitude spectrum.
\end{itemize}

Thus the canonical universe family


\[
\mathcal{U}_{\mathrm{canon}}
=
\left\{
\phi_\ast \;\middle|\;
C_{\min} < C[\phi_\ast] < C_{\max}
\right\}
\]


