=
f(r,t)
\left(
1 + \sum_{\ell,m} a_{\ell m}(t) Y_{\ell m}(\hat{x})
\right).
\]



The canonical PDE becomes a dynamical system for the amplitudes:


\[
\frac{d a_{\ell m}}{dt}
=
F_{\ell m}(a_{\ell m},\{a_{\ell' m'}\}).
\]



\subsection{Stochastic Canonical Universes}

Introduce noise:


\[
\frac{\partial\phi}{\partial t}
=
F_{\mathrm{canon}}(\phi,\nabla\phi)
+
\eta(x,t),
\]


where $\eta$ is Gaussian white noise.

This generates a statistical ensemble of universes.

